       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID. PB231PTRL.
      *> kb/Work PB231 - A BASED RECORD WITH A POINTER-CLASS LEAF IS
      *> ORDINARY, CELL-BACKED STORAGE. IT RETIRES THE LAST OF THE
      *> THREE BOUNDARIES conformance:negative/pb164-based-national-leaf
      *> PINNED - THE FIRST WAS THE USAGE BIT ONE
      *> (2002/pb231_based_bit_leaf), THE SECOND THE NATIONAL ONE
      *> (2002/pb231_based_national_leaf) - THE SAME WAY
      *> 2023/stepd_based_comp_leaf RETIRED pb151-based-comp-leaf: THE
      *> BIND-TIME COBOLNET1695 WAS REJECTING LEGAL COBOL, AND THAT
      *> FIXTURE IS DELETED IN THIS CHANGE SET.
      *> THE DERIVATION IS ONE-DIRECTIONAL AND USES NO ORACLE:
      *>   13.18.5.3 SR1/SR2 - THE ONLY RESTRICTIONS ON THE SUBJECT OF
      *>   A BASED ENTRY ARE "THE SUBJECT OF THE ENTRY SHALL NOT BE OF
      *>   CLASS OBJECT" AND "SHALL NOT BE A DYNAMIC-LENGTH ELEMENTARY
      *>   ITEM OR A VARIABLE-LENGTH GROUP". A DATA-POINTER ITEM IS OF
      *>   CLASS POINTER, NOT CLASS OBJECT, SO SR1 ADMITS IT - AND THE
      *>   ASYMMETRY IS THE STANDARD'S OWN: 13.18.22.3 SR4 BARS BOTH
      *>   CLASSES FROM THE *EXTERNAL* CLAUSE ("THE EXTERNAL CLAUSE
      *>   SHALL NOT BE SPECIFIED FOR A DATA ITEM OF CLASS OBJECT OR
      *>   POINTER") WHILE THE BASED RULE NAMES ONLY ONE. BOTH ARE
      *>   SCREENED IN THIS CHANGE SET (COBOLNET1797 / COBOLNET1796);
      *>   BEFORE IT, THE RESIDUE DIAGNOSTIC REJECTED ALL THREE SHAPES
      *>   FOR ONE WRONG REASON.
      *>   14.9.3.3 SR1 - ALLOCATE'S ONLY DEMAND ON data-name-1 IS
      *>   "THE DATA ITEM REFERENCED BY data-name-1 SHALL BE DESCRIBED
      *>   WITH THE BASED CLAUSE".
      *>   13.18.60.3 SR14 - THE TWO REACHABLE SPELLINGS: "A USAGE
      *>   CLAUSE WITH THE MESSAGE-TAG, OBJECT REFERENCE, POINTER,
      *>   FUNCTION-POINTER, OR PROGRAM-POINTER PHRASE MAY BE SPECIFIED
      *>   ONLY FOR AN ELEMENTARY DATA ITEM AT LEVEL 1 OR AN ELEMENTARY
      *>   DATA ITEM SUBORDINATE TO A TYPE DECLARATION THAT INCLUDES
      *>   THE STRONG PHRASE". BOTH ARE EXERCISED BELOW; A `05 L USAGE
      *>   POINTER` UNDER AN ORDINARY GROUP IS REJECTED COBOLNET1724 AT
      *>   THE DECLARATION AND NEVER REACHES STORAGE AT ALL.
      *> THE STORAGE MODEL. A POINTER-CLASS ITEM HOLDS A MANAGED
      *> REFERENCE, WHICH IS NOT A BYTE SEQUENCE, SO IT DOES NOT RIDE
      *> THE SHARED AREA'S BYTES: IT RIDES THE SAME AREA'S MANAGED SLOT
      *> AT THE SAME BYTE OFFSET, AND ITS BYTES THERE ARE RESERVED
      *> PLACEHOLDER POSITIONS. THAT KEEPS 14.9.3.4 GR3 - "THE AMOUNT
      *> OF STORAGE TO BE ALLOCATED IS THE NUMBER OF BYTES REQUIRED TO
      *> HOLD AN ITEM AS DESCRIBED BY data-name-1" - EXACTLY WHAT A
      *> BYTE-ADDRESSED AREA SAYS IT IS. COBOL.NET PINS EVERY
      *> POINTER/PROGRAM-POINTER/OBJECT-REFERENCE ITEM AT 8 BYTES (THE
      *> 64-BIT MANAGED CARRIER; 13.18.60.4 GR23 LEAVES THE SIZE TO THE
      *> IMPLEMENTOR - "EACH IMPLEMENTOR DEFINES THE PRECISE EFFECT OF
      *> THE USAGE POINTER CLAUSE UPON ALIGNMENT, SIZE, REPRESENTATION,
      *> AND RANGE OF VALUES OF THE DATA ITEM IN THE STORAGE OF THE
      *> COMPUTER"), SO ALLOCATE OF THE LEVEL-1 P OBTAINS
      *> AN EIGHT-BYTE CELL. THE WINDOW W PIC X(8) PROVES IT: A SHORTER
      *> CELL WOULD RAISE EC-BOUND-PTR AT THE DEREFERENCE (13.18.5.4
      *> GR4), AND W(8:1) READS THE LAST BYTE P OCCUPIES.
      *> THE RESERVED BYTES ARE READ WITH FUNCTION ORD (15.70.1: "THE
      *> ORDINAL POSITION OF argument-1 IN THE PROGRAM COLLATING
      *> SEQUENCE. THE LOWEST ORDINAL POSITION IS 1", SO ORD IS THE
      *> BYTE VALUE + 1). THEY READ 33 - THE SPACE, 0x20 - BOTH BEFORE
      *> AND AFTER P IS GIVEN A REAL ADDRESS, WHICH IS THE ASSERTION
      *> THAT THE VALUE IS NOT IN THE IMAGE. THE ADDRESS ITSELF IS
      *> PROVED REAL BY DEREFERENCING IT: WS-U, A SECOND BASED ITEM
      *> POINTED AT WHATEVER P HOLDS, READS WS-T'S CONTENT.
      *> GR9 IS OBSERVED WITHOUT THE INITIALIZED PHRASE: "IF THE
      *> INITIALIZED PHRASE IS NOT SPECIFIED AND data-name-1 IS
      *> SPECIFIED, DATA ITEMS OF CLASS OBJECT OR CLASS POINTER IN THE
      *> ALLOCATED STORAGE ARE INITIALIZED TO NULL". P READS NULL
      *> IMMEDIATELY AFTER ITS PLAIN ALLOCATE.
      *> GR4a AND GR4b ARE BOTH OBSERVED AND ARE OBSERVED TO BE THE
      *> SAME STORAGE: THE RETURNING POINTER WS-A ADDRESSES THE CELL P
      *> IS ALSO BOUND TO, AND Q - A SECOND BASED POINTER ITEM SET TO
      *> THAT SAME ADDRESS - SHARES P'S SLOT. SETTING Q TO NULL IS
      *> VISIBLE THROUGH P, WHICH IS WHAT MAKES THE SLOT PART OF THE
      *> STORAGE AREA RATHER THAN OF THE ITEM.
      *> THE STRONG-TYPE SPELLING (SR14'S SECOND ARM) EXERCISES A
      *> POINTER *MEMBER*: GR9 SEEDS IT NULL, IT ROUND-TRIPS A REAL
      *> ADDRESS, AND THE ALPHANUMERIC MEMBER BESIDE IT KEEPS ITS OWN
      *> CONTENT - THE TWO HALVES OF ONE AREA. ITS BYTE QUANTITY IS NOT
      *> SEPARATELY OBSERVABLE HERE AND DELIBERATELY IS NOT ASSERTED: A
      *> BYTE WINDOW OVER A STRONGLY-TYPED RECORD WOULD NEED
      *> `SET ADDRESS OF <UNTYPED> TO <RESTRICTED POINTER>`, WHICH
      *> 14.9.39.3 SR19 FORBIDS ("IF identifier-6 REFERENCES A
      *> RESTRICTED DATA-POINTER, EITHER identifier-5 SHALL REFERENCE A
      *> DATA-POINTER RESTRICTED TO THE SAME TYPE OR data-name-1 SHALL
      *> BE A TYPED ITEM OF THE TYPE TO WHICH identifier-6 IS
      *> RESTRICTED"), AND 8.4.3.11.4 GR2 MAKES `ADDRESS OF R`
      *> RESTRICTED. THE 8-BYTE RESERVATION IS THE SAME ONE LAW THE
      *> LEVEL-1 CASE PINS.
      *> GR7 IS EXERCISED ON THE STRONG RECORD: "IF BOTH THE
      *> INITIALIZED PHRASE AND data-name-1 ARE SPECIFIED, THE
      *> ALLOCATED STORAGE IS INITIALIZED AS IF AN INITIALIZE
      *> data-name-1 WITH FILLER ALL TO VALUE THEN TO DEFAULT STATEMENT
      *> WERE EXECUTED". T-N CARRIES A VALUE AND TAKES IT (ALL TO
      *> VALUE); T-P DOES NOT, SO IT TAKES 14.9.20.4 GR6c's DEFAULT
      *> SENDING-OPERAND FOR ITS CATEGORY, WHICH THAT RULE'S TABLE
      *> GIVES AS "PREDEFINED ADDRESS NULL" FOR DATA-POINTER - AND
      *> 14.9.20.4 SPELLS THE IMPLICIT STATEMENT FOR SUCH A RECEIVER AS
      *> A SET, NOT A MOVE. A POINTER GIVEN A REAL ADDRESS FIRST IS
      *> OBSERVED TO GO BACK TO NULL.
      *> FREE TAKES THE POINTER, NOT THE RECORD (14.9.15.3 SR1 - "THE
      *> DATA ITEM REFERENCED BY data-name-1 SHALL BE OF CATEGORY
      *> DATA-POINTER"), AND RELEASES BOTH HALVES OF THE AREA
      *> (14.9.15.4 GR1a - "THE CONTENTS OF ANY DATA ITEMS LOCATED
      *> WITHIN THE RELEASED STORAGE AREA BECOME UNDEFINED").
       DATA DIVISION.
       WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
       01 T-PTR IS TYPEDEF STRONG.
          05 T-P USAGE POINTER.
          05 T-N PIC X(4) VALUE "VVVV".
       01 R TYPE T-PTR BASED.
       01 P USAGE POINTER BASED.
       01 Q USAGE POINTER BASED.
       01 W PIC X(8) BASED.
       01 WS-A USAGE POINTER.
       01 WS-B USAGE POINTER.
       01 WS-T PIC X(4) VALUE "ABCD".
       01 WS-U PIC X(4) BASED.
       PROCEDURE DIVISION.
       MAIN.
      *> GR4a + GR4b: ONE ALLOCATE, TWO ADDRESSES, ONE STORAGE.
           ALLOCATE P RETURNING WS-A
           SET ADDRESS OF W TO WS-A
      *> GR9 - the plain ALLOCATE seeds a class-pointer item to null.
           IF P = NULL
              DISPLAY "GR9=NULL"
           ELSE
              DISPLAY "GR9=SET"
           END-IF
      *> GR3's byte quantity: the eight-byte window derefs, and its
      *> bytes are the reserved placeholders, before and after.
           DISPLAY "PRE=" FUNCTION ORD(W(1:1)) " " FUNCTION ORD(W(8:1))
           SET P TO ADDRESS OF WS-T
           DISPLAY "POST=" FUNCTION ORD(W(1:1)) " "
               FUNCTION ORD(W(8:1))
      *> The slot holds a REAL address - dereference it.
           SET ADDRESS OF WS-U TO P
           DISPLAY "DEREF=[" WS-U "]"
      *> The slot belongs to the AREA: a second based pointer item over
      *> the same cell is the same value, in both directions.
           SET ADDRESS OF Q TO WS-A
           SET WS-B TO Q
           SET ADDRESS OF WS-U TO WS-B
           DISPLAY "ALIAS=[" WS-U "]"
           SET Q TO NULL
           IF P = NULL
              DISPLAY "SHARED=YES"
           ELSE
              DISPLAY "SHARED=NO"
           END-IF
           FREE WS-A
      *> SR14's STRONG arm: a pointer MEMBER beside an alphanumeric one.
           ALLOCATE R
           IF T-P IN R = NULL
              DISPLAY "MGR9=NULL"
           ELSE
              DISPLAY "MGR9=SET"
           END-IF
           MOVE "WXYZ" TO T-N IN R
           SET T-P IN R TO ADDRESS OF WS-T
           SET WS-B TO T-P IN R
           SET ADDRESS OF WS-U TO WS-B
           DISPLAY "MEMBER=[" T-N IN R "] MDEREF=[" WS-U "]"
      *> GR7 - ALL TO VALUE for T-N, THEN TO DEFAULT for T-P, whose
      *> 14.9.20.4 GR6c default is the predefined address NULL.
           INITIALIZE R WITH FILLER ALL TO VALUE THEN TO DEFAULT
           IF T-P IN R = NULL
              DISPLAY "GR7=NULL"
           ELSE
              DISPLAY "GR7=SET"
           END-IF
           DISPLAY "GR7N=[" T-N IN R "]"
           STOP RUN.
